==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|legal|US}} The right of a [[government]] over the private property within its [[jurisdiction]]. Usually [[invoke]]d to compel land owners to sell their property in preparation for a major construction project such as a [[freeway]].
#: ''The city council used '''eminent domain''' to make me sell my store.''
# {{lb|en|historical}} In [[feudalism]], the legal interest or rights of a [[lord]] or [[superior]] in an [[estate in land]] held in [[fee]], as opposed to the vassal's or tenant's interest.

====Synonyms====
# {{l|en|compulsory purchase}} {{a|UK|Ireland|New Zealand}}, [[compulsory acquisition]] {{a|Australia}}, [[expropriation]] {{a|Canada|South Africa}}
# [[superiority]] {{qualifier|Scots law}}

====Antonyms====
* {{lb|en|feudal law}}: [[utile domain]], [[inferiority]] (Scots law)

